{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":26516,"name":"Hayden","username":"TranNhi27","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/talk.nervos.org/trannhi27/{size}/11777_2.png","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:28:35.904Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi everyone!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’ve been working on FiberSurvivors, a top-down survivors-like (kinda like Vampire Survivors) that runs in the browser, where the CKB you earn and the upgrade cards you buy are all paid over Fiber.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo a run goes like this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou open the game and a Fiber node starts in your browser, with its own wallet\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou fund it from the testnet faucet\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePress Play, and the game opens a channel to the hub node (game’s reward liquidity)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClear a level, and the hub pays you CKB\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBuy upgrade cards mid-run by paying an invoice\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCash out at the end, the channel closes and your CKB goes back on-chain\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll you need is a browser tab, no extension, no local node, no CLI. Everything runs on testnet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Loop Graph:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode class=\"lang-auto\"\u003efund a channel ──► fight through 10 levels ──► hub pays each level cleared\n                              ▲                             │\n                              │                             ▼\n                       stronger build ◄──── spend earnings on upgrade cards\n                              │\n                              ▼\n                   cash out ──► channel closes, CKB settles on-chain\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo it’s more rewards vs more power. You earn more if you buy fewer cards, kite well and win, but if you lose a level, the run ends there. Right now there are 10 levels with a dragon boss at the end, more might come later.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-motivation-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-motivation-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eMotivation\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile learning Fiber and CKB, I felt like Fiber fits PvP games best, since two players can pay each other directly over a channel, so you don’t have to put all the trust on one server. But for UX, I wanted players to have a smooth experience without setting up a local node or finding someone to match with, and on a testnet demo it’s pretty hard to find another player online. So in the end it became a single-player game where you earn CKB by playing and spend it on upgrades, at least for now.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/7/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5_2_213x375.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"gWXkMzepGoeHv3ntysxsTgAjhKB\" width=\"213\" height=\"375\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5_2_213x375.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5_2_319x562.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/7/76cce6193a6300abd4b173bfe57e130572970bf5_2_426x750.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"7AA2C3\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e735×1287 126 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/2/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/2/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097_2_216x375.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"6pXc0akpFhVVqt2bgqbSFP8T1EX\" width=\"216\" height=\"375\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/2/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097_2_216x375.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/2/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097_2_324x562.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/2/2cfc2124c19b82041f79a3e0466e68690e797097_2_432x750.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"7EACA5\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e746×1293 167 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/4/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f_2_215x375.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"agGrj70Qk0ugjbAWxeMG4JcsNav\" width=\"215\" height=\"375\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f_2_215x375.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f_2_322x562.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/4/47f88faf0fe81fc25c5330129a181204d2f5488f_2_430x750.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"4F706F\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e748×1302 170 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e \u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/original/2X/a/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3\" title=\"image\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/a/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3_2_236x375.jpeg\" alt=\"image\" data-base62-sha1=\"oq4oLmlzLZnwmM7MzxUjVEUNQll\" width=\"236\" height=\"375\" srcset=\"https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/a/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3_2_236x375.jpeg, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/a/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3_2_354x562.jpeg 1.5x, https://talk.nervos.org/uploads/default/optimized/2X/a/ab269fcbaf99f94914bb2a657504a25fcf3478b3_2_472x750.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"819465\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003eimage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e807×1280 113 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-try-it-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-try-it-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eTry it\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDemo: \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://zesty-youtiao-8586ae.netlify.app\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003ehttps://zesty-youtiao-8586ae.netlify.app\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSDK repo: \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/TranNhi27/FiberWebGLSDK\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eFiber WebGL SDK\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe game source isn’t public since it uses some paid assets (Feel and the Vefects Effect Pack), and their licenses don’t allow sharing them. But all the Fiber parts are in the SDK, which is fully open.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-how-it-works-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-how-it-works-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow it works\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe game is built in Unity (WebGL). For the Fiber part I use my own Fiber WebGL SDK, which runs Fiber’s WASM node (\u003ccode\u003e@nervosnetwork/fiber-js\u003c/code\u003e) inside the build.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the other side there’s one \u003ccode\u003efnn\u003c/code\u003e node (the hub) on a small cloud VM, plus a small Express server next to it. Every player opens one channel to the hub, and all rewards and card payments go through it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe server is the one deciding money, not the client:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRewards:\u003c/strong\u003e The coins you pick up only count once you reach the exit. That’s when the client claims them, the server checks the claim, and the hub pays you. Die before the exit and those coins are gone. The full campaign is 10 levels and pays up to 216 CKB\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCards:\u003c/strong\u003e When you buy a card, the client only sends the card id. The server makes an invoice with the price, then the client decodes it and checks the price matches what it showed you before paying. Cards are 5 to 45 CKB, so if you buy a lot you can actually end a run with less than you started with lol\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCash out:\u003c/strong\u003e Cash out closes the channel and settles both sides on-chain\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach player channel is 400 CKB, and the hub puts in 400 CKB on its side too.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-the-sdk-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-the-sdk-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eThe SDK\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile building this I ended up turning all the Fiber stuff into a Unity package, which I submitted to the \u003ca href=\"https://talk.nervos.org/t/gone-in-60ms-fiber-network-infrastructure-hackathon-announcement/10418\"\u003eGone in 60ms\u003c/a\u003e Hackathon where my winning chances were also gone in 60ms \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/images/emoji/apple/face_holding_back_tears.png?v=15\" title=\":face_holding_back_tears:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":face_holding_back_tears:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnyway, any Unity WebGL game can use it too:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eIPaymentGateway\u003c/code\u003e: start the node, connect, open/close channels, keysend\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eIInvoicePaymentGateway\u003c/code\u003e: decode an invoice, check the amount, pay\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eIUdtPaymentGateway\u003c/code\u003e: xUDT channels and payments, route dry-runs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eIFiberWallet\u003c/code\u003e: on-chain CKB balance\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eIFiberDiagnostics\u003c/code\u003e: peers and channels\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere’s a sample scene in the repo if you want to try it without the game.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-limitations-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-limitations-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eLimitations\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWell, to be honest this is a tech demo for “a Fiber node inside a Unity browser game”. The money side is protected: the client never decides an amount, rewards come from the server, and card prices come in server-made invoices. But the gameplay itself isn’t verified \u003cimg src=\"https://talk.nervos.org/images/emoji/apple/sweat_smile.png?v=15\" title=\":sweat_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sweat_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYou trust the server\u003c/strong\u003e: The server can’t see the gameplay itself, but it rejects claims that are out of order, too fast, or have more coins than the level could drop. With one claim per level per session and a payout cap per player, that’s what stops reward spamming for now, but there’s no real anti-cheat.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe key lives in the browser\u003c/strong\u003e: Like any Fiber node, it signs automatically, but here the key is kept in the browser’s \u003ccode\u003elocalStorage\u003c/code\u003e for this site. If you clear your site data, the key and any CKB in it are gone. That’s okay for testnet, but letting players back up the key, or binding it to their own CKB wallet, would fix this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOpening a channel takes a few minutes\u003c/strong\u003e on testnet since it waits for on-chain confirmation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-how-to-play-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-how-to-play-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eHow to play\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere’s a tutorial in the game, but here are the controls:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eControls:\u003c/strong\u003e WASD to move, attacks are automatic, 1 to 4 to use a skill, left-click to aim, right-click to cancel.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-some-tips-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-some-tips-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSome tips\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf the channel open fails, wait a minute and try again, testnet can be slow sometimes\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDon’t forget to cash out at the end to get your CKB back on-chain\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-26516-credits-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-26516-credits-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eCredits\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKudos to these free assets, they helped me build this a lot faster:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://kaylousberg.itch.io/\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eKayKit’s Packs\u003c/a\u003e for my game including Characters, Skeleton Enemies, Environment, Animations\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMy cute \u003ca href=\"https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/3d/characters/creatures/dragon-for-boss-monster-pbr-78923\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eDragon Boss\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/2d/gui/icons/space-game-gui-kit-298577\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003eSpace Game GUI Kit\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003